INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Mandiant 3CX supply-chain investigation; Kaspersky Gopuram analysis; WIRED synthesis", "source_url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/3cx-software-supply-chain-compromise", "text": "Evidence chain: Mandiant reported that the initial compromise vector into 3CX was malicious software downloaded from the Trading Technologies website, specifically a tampered X_TRADER installer from an earlier software supply-chain compromise. A 3CX employee installed the compromised X_TRADER, which enabled access to spread through the 3CX network, reach software-development/build servers, and corrupt the 3CX installer. Mandiant reconstructed credential harvesting and lateral movement; both Windows and macOS build environments were compromised. Windows build environment: TAXHAUL launcher and COLDCAT downloader, DLL search-order hijacking through IKEEXT, LocalSystem. macOS build server: POOLRAT backdoor with Launch Daemons; earlier reporting called it SIMPLESEA, but Mandiant determined the sample was POOLRAT. The poisoned 3CX DesktopApp 18.12.416 and earlier distributed SUDDENICON, which obtained C2 URLs from encrypted GitHub icon files and downloaded ICONICSTEALER, a browser-information dataminer. Mandiant tracks activity as UNC4736, a suspected North Korean nexus cluster, and assesses with moderate confidence that UNC4736 is related to financially motivated North Korean AppleJeus activity; evidence included POOLRAT overlap with a CISA-reported trojanized CoinGoTrade AppleJeus sample and infrastructure links. Mandiant states this was a cascading supply-chain compromise. Kaspersky reported trojanized MSI/macOS installers, malicious DLL decrypting shellcode from d3dcompiler_47.dll overlay, GitHub-hosted icon C2 extraction, infostealer collection of system information/browser history, and Gopuram backdoor deployments. Kaspersky attributed the campaign to Lazarus with medium-to-high confidence based on Gopuram coexisting with AppleJeus on a prior cryptocurrency-company infection, cryptocurrency targeting, shared loader shellcode and a C2 previously linked to AppleJeus, and oilycargo domain attribution. Kaspersky said fewer than ten machines received Gopuram, indicating surgical targeting. WIRED reported Mandiant's patient-zero narrative and described public aliases Kimsuky, Emerald Sleet, and Velvet Chollima, but this naming differs from Mandiant's UNC4736 and is an attribution/alias discrepancy rather than proof of separate actors. Google TAG source described earlier Operation AppleJeus activity as North Korean government-backed activity targeting cryptocurrency/fintech and compromised Trading Technologies website in February 2022, including hidden iframes and Chrome exploit activity; Mandiant used this as corroboration, not as direct proof of the 3CX intrusion."}
